// REJECTS: Unexpected token '}'. Valid alternatives: ['->subType(@']
//
// A graph fetch subtree must fetch SOMETHING. `Class { }` is not "fetch the class with no
// properties", it is unparseable -- and the single alternative offered says why: at that
// position the grammar wants a property name or the root-level cast, and has no empty
// alternative to fall back on.
//
// Empty collections are the classic accidental permission. A rewrite writing `while (not
// '}') parseProperty()` accepts the empty body for free, without a decision ever being
// made, and emits a tree node with zero subtrees that serialises fine and fetches nothing.
###Pure
function fixture::neg::emptyTree(): meta::pure::metamodel::type::Any[*]
{
   #{
      fixture::neg::Catalog {
      }
   }#
}
